  "observed_behavior": [
    "Exact schema/mcpServers and type-specific fields validated. stdio and streamable-http normalize distinctly; missing/unknown types and SSE yield named per-server errors while valid declaration siblings remain visible. Runtime still rejects the whole invalid configuration.",
    "HTTP URL validation rejects user information, fragments, non-HTTP(S), and non-loopback HTTP. Header names/values and case-insensitive duplicates validate before all client-owned headers are stripped; preserved custom headers normalize to http_headers.",
    "Portable stdio command/args/env/cwd types and reserved names validate. Default cwd remains explicit ${PLUGIN_ROOT}; placeholders are retained unexpanded for task 16. Runtime rejects the still-unimplemented cwd/header/env-reference settings instead of dropping them.",
    "Package format is authoritative. Portable manifests require strict mcp.json; legacy packages retain command/url inference even with schema metadata. Missing optional portable mcp.json is skipped, disabled packages do not contribute, and previously audited package/overlay paths are reaudited for links.",
    "Independent .codex-plugin overlay can add only local env_vars to existing same-name stdio declarations, even if root com.openai inline metadata exists. It cannot replace commands/args/cwd/URL, change HTTP transport, add servers, or import remote references. Matching literal env placeholders are removed only for corresponding local references."
  ],
  "intentional_safety_differences": [
    "Existing host component policy rejects all parent components, Windows drive spellings and symlink components; it remains stricter than the snapshot's contained-parent path normalization. No path policy is weakened.",
